{"author":{"id":"585844baa6074d44d241f46aa7c9f21ff46653adf617d7f070fbfe327626c989"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794837180,"nonce":"gdCv9xFlGwBETAuOxb96xPiKv4k=","title":"A #[hxn(blocking)] method with a #[hxn::data] parameter generates an adapter that does not compile","message":"hxn-gen wraps the call of a #[hxn(blocking)] method in `blocking(|| ...)`, and decodes a #[hxn::data] argument inside that closure with `?`. The decoder's error type is `Fault`, while the closure returns the method's `Result\u003c_, String\u003e`, so rustc fails with E0277 (\"`?` couldn't convert the error to `String`\").\n\nSeen in hxn-gpu-vulkan, when a doc comment and #[hxn(blocking)] ended up above `Device.create_swapchain(\u0026self, surface: \u0026Surface, width: i32, height: i32, format: Format, vsync: bool)`, where Format is a #[hxn::data] enum. The generated HashLink adapter, at line 727 of the crate hxn builds, read:\n\n    Ok(manage(blocking(|| this.create_swapchain(\u0026surface, width, height, hxn_read_format(format)?, vsync))?))\n\nFix: decode data arguments into locals before the blocking closure, as the comment there says is done for everything else the call reads (\"Everything the call reads was copied or borrowed above\", crates/hxn-gen/src/rust.rs). Add a generate test: a blocking method taking a data enum.","files":null}]}